{
  "sticker": "seaweed",
  "skeleton": "seaweed growing from a little rock, facing the viewer: root at the holdfast (on the ground); body (pivot at the holdfast) carrying every frond; each frond on its own bone at its base so it sways and waves (frondFace with the face, frondTall, frondRight, frondLeft, frondTop); face on the face frond with eyes, mouth and brows; the holdfast in front.",
  "sheets": [
    {
      "id": "parts",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a smiling seaweed character: green kelp fronds growing from a little brown rock. Draw this exact seaweed as a cut-out paper puppet: its separate body parts laid out on one sheet, the same drawing style, colours, texture, line and proportions as in image 1, every part at the size it has in image 1.\n\nDraw each part on its own, spread out over the sheet with wide empty gaps between them, no part touching or overlapping another:\n1. the holdfast: the little brown rock clump with its roots at the bottom of image 1, alone.\n2. the face frond: the big wide green frond with the face, left of the middle in image 1, from its narrow stem end at the bottom to its curled tip, with a completely blank face — no eyes, no mouth — keep the rosy cheeks.\n3. the tall frond: the tallest frond, in the middle of image 1, from its narrow stem end at the bottom to its curled tip at the top.\n4. the right frond: the yellow-green wavy frond on the right of image 1, from its narrow stem end at the bottom to its tip, with its round golden air bladder.\n5. the left curl: the frond curling out to the far left of image 1, from its narrow stem end to its curled tip.\n6. the top-left frond: the frond at the top left of image 1 with its curled tip, from its narrow stem end, with its thin stalk of round golden air bladders.\n\nEvery part is drawn whole, including what is normally hidden behind another part, and each joint end (where it tucks under the body or another part) is a full, smooth, rounded edge. No text, no labels, no numbers, no outline around the parts beyond the drawing's own line, no shadows. Fully transparent background."
    },
    {
      "id": "face",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "references": [
        "parts"
      ],
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a smiling seaweed character: green kelp fronds growing from a little brown rock; image 2 shows the same seaweed cut into puppet parts, with a blank face. Draw the seaweed's face pieces as separate stickers on one sheet: the same drawing style, colours and line as in image 1, every piece at the size it has on the seaweed in image 1, so it fits the blank face in image 2.\n\nDraw each piece on its own, spread out in tidy rows with wide empty gaps between them, nothing touching:\n1. the left eye (on the right of image 1) as it is in image 1: a small dark eye with a white sparkle and a few lashes.\n2. the same eye wide open and surprised: bigger and rounder, with its white sparkle.\n3. the same eye gently closed in sleep: a soft downward-curving line with a few lashes.\n4. the same eye closed in a happy smile: an upward-curving arc.\n5. the same eye sad: looking down, its upper lid tilted up towards the middle.\n6. the same eye squeezed shut, crying: a tight, creased, downward-curving closed line.\n7. the mouth as it is in image 1: a small happy smile line.\n8. the mouth wide open in a big happy laugh, the inside pink.\n9. the mouth open in a small round 'o'.\n10. the mouth in a small sad frown.\n11. the mouth open in a wobbly crying wail, its corners turned down, the inside pink.\n12. one eyebrow: a small, thin, softly curved dark brown line.\n\nNo text, no labels, no numbers, no shadows, no face or head around the pieces. Fully transparent background."
    }
  ],
